        "text": "Investors sometimes make the mistake of memorizing phrases from marketing materials without truly understanding them. Officers are experienced at hearing rehearsed answers that do not match follow up questions. In our preparation sessions, we help clients translate complex project structures into their own words so they can explain, for example, that they invested in a new commercial enterprise which then loans money to a job creating entity that is building a hotel, or another type of project, in a way that feels natural and accurate."
