        "text": "For many families, especially those whose first language is not English, describing these plans and histories can feel more challenging than discussing numbers. A short answer that might sound polite in one culture can appear evasive in a U.S. interview. Likewise, a family member who answers for the principal investor, even with good intentions, can give the impression that the investor does not fully understand their own finances or project."
